			"type": "text",
			"text": "Yanornis is a bird discovered from Jiufotang Formation and Yixian Formation with both formations housing different species dating back to the Early Cretaceous. Its name means 'yan bird' as a reference to the Yan feudal fiefdom, one of the many Chinese dynasties. It was a little longer than 30 centimeters long, being aroun the size of modern pigeons. From stomach contents we know that these birds were piscivores, feeding on fish."
